Say a GPU context failed a few times, not thirty thousand.

A device that could not create a GL context produced about 32000 copies
each of three lines within a minute of starting:

  ContextResult::kFatalFailure: Failed to create shared context for
  virtualization.
  SharedImageStub: unable to create context
  GpuChannel: Failed to create SharedImageStub

Each retry is a channel being re-established, and the retrying is worth
keeping: it is the same path a context lost at runtime comes back
through, which this port depends on (see
ohos-gpu-context-lost-recovery.patch). Latching the first fatal result
and refusing to try again would turn a recoverable loss into a permanent
white page.

What is not worth keeping is saying so every time. The first few say
everything the hundredth does, and at this rate the interesting lines
around them -- what ANGLE said when the display failed -- scroll out of
the log before anyone can read them.

So: the first three, then every thousandth, each carrying its count so
the rate is still visible.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_manager.cc b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_manager.cc
--- a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_manager.cc
+++ b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel_manager.cc
@@ -954,9 +954,16 @@ scoped_refptr<SharedContextState> GpuChannelManager::GetSharedContextState(
     if (!context) {
       // TODO(piman): This might not be fatal, we could recurse into
       // CreateGLContext to get more info, tho it should be exceedingly
       // rare and may not be recoverable anyway.
-      LOG(ERROR) << "ContextResult::kFatalFailure: "
-                    "Failed to create shared context for virtualization.";
+      // Exceedingly rare it is not, when GL never came up at all: every
+      // channel that is established tries again. Say the first few and
+      // then thin it out, so what ANGLE said stays readable.
+      static int failures = 0;
+      if (++failures <= 3 || failures % 1000 == 0) {
+        LOG(ERROR) << "ContextResult::kFatalFailure: "
+                      "Failed to create shared context for virtualization. ("
+                   << failures << ")";
+      }
       *result = ContextResult::kFatalFailure;
       return nullptr;
     }
diff --git a/gpu/ipc/service/shared_image_stub.cc b/gpu/ipc/service/shared_image_stub.cc
--- a/gpu/ipc/service/shared_image_stub.cc
+++ b/gpu/ipc/service/shared_image_stub.cc
@@ -590,7 +590,11 @@ ContextResult SharedImageStub::Initialize() {
     ContextResult result;
     context_state_ = channel_manager->GetSharedContextState(&result);
     if (result != ContextResult::kSuccess) {
-      LOG(ERROR) << "SharedImageStub: unable to create context";
+      static int failures = 0;
+      if (++failures <= 3 || failures % 1000 == 0) {
+        LOG(ERROR) << "SharedImageStub: unable to create context ("
+                   << failures << ")";
+      }
       context_state_ = nullptr;
       return result;
     }
diff --git a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel.cc b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel.cc
--- a/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel.cc
+++ b/gpu/ipc/service/gpu_channel.cc
@@ -784,5 +784,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<GpuChannel> GpuChannel::Create(

   if (!gpu_channel->CreateSharedImageStub(gpu_extra_info)) {
-    LOG(ERROR) << "GpuChannel: Failed to create SharedImageStub";
+    static int failures = 0;
+    if (++failures <= 3 || failures % 1000 == 0) {
+      LOG(ERROR) << "GpuChannel: Failed to create SharedImageStub ("
+                 << failures << ")";
+    }
     return nullptr;
   }
   return gpu_channel;
